# The object of the definition is a parameter of a function that code nobody sees may call: the object may be its own, so what a written descriptor lays on it goes out of sight, though every object that the program itself hands in is of a layout in sight. L0 = what is laid.
# RUN: link layouts mechanisms=all
# CHECK: layout L0 changes=[IsFrozen, GainsProperty, LosesProperty, ChangesPrototype, GetsAccessor]
